<title>USA: USDA June 12 world grain highlights.</title>
<headline>USDA June 12 world grain highlights.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Global grain production in 1997/98 was forecast at 1,855.05 million tonnes, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>Last month, the estimate was 1,854.61 million tonnes.</p>
<p>World output would include 578.82 million tonnes of wheat, 898.93 million of coarse (feed) grains and 377.31 million of rice. Oilseeds were pegged at 273.00 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The EU wheat crop this year was forecast for 97.85 million tonnes, same as the May estimate. Drought hit the crop early in the year.  </p>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 soybean crop was estimated at 26.50 million tonnes, a record. Exports for the marketing year were put at 7.50 million tonnes, up one million tonnes.</p>
<p>EU wheat exports in 1997/98 were forecast for 31.23 million tonnes. Exports from Canada were pegged for 19.00 million and Australia 14.00 million.</p>
<p>China's imports during 1996/97 were estimated at 1.50 million tonnes of soyoil, 2.70 million of soymeal, 2.10 million of soybeans and 3.00 million of wheat. In the same period, it was forecast to export 2.50 million tonnes of corn.</p>
